\f0\b\fs24 \cf2 Applying Transformative Game\
Design Theory to Competitive Debate\
\pard\pardeftab720\sb100\sa100\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Pass with Distinction (pending revisions)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sb100\sa100\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf2 This is an ambitious, intellectually mature, and highly original thesis that tackles an unusual research problem with impressive rigor and creativity. The work successfully bridges debate studies, game design, and transformative role-playing theory, resulting in a contribution that feels genuinely novel and potentially relevant far beyond the immediate context of competitive debate. Particularly impressive are the quality of the literature review, the depth of the design process documentation, and the way the project generates practical design knowledge through research-through-design. The thesis demonstrates a strong command of both theory and design practice, and several of its most interesting insights, especially regarding transformation, facilitation, and emancipatory forms of play, have implications that extend into education, mediation, therapy, and other interpersonal contexts.\
The revisions below are largely concerned with sharpening and foregrounding contributions that are already present in the thesis. In many cases, the strongest arguments have already been developed; the task now is to bring them forward more consistently, strengthen evidential support, and align the structure around the central "how" question that drives the project. If these revisions are implemented, this thesis is comfortably at the level of a Pass with Distinction.\
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Revisions\
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf0 - add abstract\
- Add proper format in cover page: name of supervisor and examiner\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Throughout thesis:\
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf0 - add examples or sources to all claims you make (e.g. \'93a very diverse range of debate formats are played all over the world\'94, \cf2 Academic debate formats are games.\'94 (Snider?): Be clear and transparent when you are building an argument yourself (e.g. \'93in this thesis, I will argue that academic debate formats are essentially games\'94)\
\cf0 - introduce and define your key terms: e.g. \'93debate\'94, \'93transformative game design\'94 etc. This should be based on sources rather than gut feeling\
- remove value judgments/anything that isn\'92t descriptive wording (e.g. \'93extreme\'94, \'93immense\'94 etc)\
- Restate the problem statement in a way that makes the research gap clearer (you repeat the gap later on in a very clear way, write a version of this as your problem statement)\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf0 Particular chapters\
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0 \cf0 - Chapter 1 is more underdeveloped than the rest of your thesis, and should be made clearer (suggestions see below) Especially 1.5. \'93\cf2 Its main contribution to knowledge is to exemplify that debate formats can be designed better if looked at as roleplaying games.\'94: Flesh this out more and elaborate: What does \'93better\'94 mean in the context of this thesis? How does the thesis explore this? Explain what \'93five evaluation fields\'94 refers to (are these categories for playtest observations?)\
\
The literature review is exceptionally well developed!\
- 2.1 is excellently written. A 1-2 sentence version of this argument should be moved to chapter 1 (motivation). Consider moving the following paragraph entirely: \'93Although forensics pedagogy has documented debate\'92s transformative effects, no prior work analyzes major debate formats from a game design perspective or applies transformative role-playing game theory to competitive debate. Addressing this gap is the central\
contribution of this thesis.\'94: This is a very clear description of your research gap, motivating the RQ.\
\
\
\cf0 - 2.2 very rich discussion, clearly structured. Third dimension of leisure community lacks sources: references/examples to important tournaments that demonstrate the community aspect. I might also be compelling to cite fan studies literature, since what you\'92re describing about debating communities sounds very similar to media culture more generally.\
\
- Design process of Inside Out (please italicise the title throughout thesis) is very well described, the design intentions reflected clearly and compellingly: goes in depth with generating design knowledge on the structure of debates as well as transformative games: Emphasise this aspect of RtD - this is a real contribution that is currently not appropriately highlighted: This thesis generates knowledge on how to potentially design for transformation in a interpersonal setting, using (and subverting) debate structure. This has relevance for other contexts as well (e.g. therapy, education, mediation). Consider adding a paragraph to the conclusion which speculates about the relevance/applicability of your design in different contexts:\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf2 - Two outstanding examples for the relevance of your work: \
\
1) The description of the evaluator is reminiscent of the role of a mediator/therapist: \'93the Evaluator explains the commendations awarded, articulates why particular moments demonstrated particular skills, and offers advice oriented toward growth rather than winning a future round\'94. Might\cf0  Inside Out be a resource for group therapy sessions, where a problem is explored via a fictional \'93subject\'94, guided by a professional mediator \'93evaluator\'94 ?\
\
2) your observations on emancipatory bleed in 6.2.1: Expand and emphasise this part! You show earlier how Inside Out subverts the binary & victory expectations of classical debate formats. Your data emphasises a link to gender (e.g. hyper-competition as a male-coded expectation in debate): Your design seems to be transformative in a feminist/anti-patriarchal way, simply by implementing procedural structures that are outside the (male-coded) box of traditional debate design. If this is a \'93surprising\'94 side effect, it is still important as an observation that\'92s part of your generated RtD knowledge.\
\
- The discussion of your RQ throughout thesis is misaligned. What you say in 1.4 is very clear and compelling. The \'93how\'94 focus should be repeated throughout the thesis, especially in 6. Focus on the how (rather than the whether) of the design process, is where the core knowledge of this thesis is located: 1) How did you go about designing such a format? 2) How did your participants respond? Ditch/rephrase any instances of yes/no (whether) answers, since they short-circuit/close the discussion.\
\
- 6.2 I recommend using the \'93how\'94 framing here, instead of \'93confirming predictions\'94 (totalising language) - In a qualitative RtD work, this is more rigorous since it allows for multiple perspective to coexist, and keeps the conversation open for future iterations.\
\
\pard\pardeftab720\sb100\sa100\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Conclusion: The last two paragraphs read a bit confusing and unclear (perhaps because of the sudden \'93epic\'94 register break). They also read unnecessarily harsh and dismissive of your compelling design contributions, complex methodology and impressive playtesting results. I recommend  writing something equally ethic that\'92s a bit more fair towards yourself and your potentially inspired readers :)\
